  data: {
    LLM: "Prioritize clearing out the first four occupied cells as quickly as possible to increase your mobility. Never move a card into a cell if you can keep it in the tableau.\n\nEmpty Columns: An empty column is more valuable than a free cell because it can hold a whole sequence of cards (starting with a King). Work toward emptying a column early.\n\nThe Suit-Lock: Since building is by same suit, if you have a high card of a suit (like a Jack) buried under a low card of the SAME suit (like a 4), that column is 'locked' until the 4 is moved. Identify and solve these suit-locks immediately.",
    Player: "Prioritize clearing out the first four occupied cells as quickly as possible to increase your mobility. Never move a card into a cell if you can keep it in the tableau.\n\nEmpty Columns: An empty column is more valuable than a free cell because it can hold a whole sequence of cards (starting with a King). Work toward emptying a column early.\n\nThe Suit-Lock: Since building is by same suit, if you have a high card of a suit (like a Jack) buried under a low card of the SAME suit (like a 4), that column is 'locked' until the 4 is moved. Identify and solve these suit-locks immediately.",
